    "requiredHumanChecks": [
      "Walk entry -> state -> council -> a child if officially applicable, and a direct detail link -> route back. Confirm understandable next choices and the same search/select/inspect/open interaction.",
      "Inspect the actual coast, islands, marine boundaries, geographic registration, colours and source credits at full-place and local zoom. Compare real source-based picks, holes and multipolygon parts.",
      "Exercise drag, zoom, reset, search/no-results, keyboard, focus, selected-area link, optional road style, narrow navigation and no-JavaScript fallback.",
      "Review every Twinkle against the canonical format: one ordinary gripe in its title, one self-contained spoken breath, systems rather than vulnerable people as the target, quiet care where appropriate, and evidence/context below.",
      "Check public source links, observation periods, boundary editions/effective dates, statistical denominators, representatives, jurisdiction-specific election law and current official election/early-voting notices.",
      "Verify clock behavior before/on/after its local date and any sourced early-voting window. Check private note handling, permissions and static archive limits.",
      "Read the local-to-system connections, lyric meanings, optional candidate/Genesis learning and the cost/freely-given/change accounts for truthful scope and coherent human choices."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Saved browser fixture results are dated evidence; the validator does not launch a browser or test a physical touch device.",
      "No review date is inferred from generation time, file modification time or a passing check.",
      "Live source freshness, law, exact address eligibility, humour and cultural authority require original-source and human review.",
      "No quantitative electorate overlap, population influence estimate, completed civic outcome or candidate announcement is inferred.",
      "Future places must supply their own source-specific counts, routes, timezone, boundaries, representatives, election rules and review evidence."
